section.legal
  .container.legal__wrap
    p.kicker.kicker--accent Legal
    h1.legal__title Privacy Policy
    p.legal__updated Last updated: September 11, 2026

    .legal__body
      p
        | This Privacy Policy explains how 
        strong Lyzfol
        |  (“we”, “us”, “our”) collects, uses, stores, and protects information when you visit and use 
        = link_to 'https://lyzfol.com/', 'https://lyzfol.com/'
        |  (the “Website”).
      p By accessing or using the Website, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy.

      h2 1. Information We Collect
      p We may collect information automatically when you visit the Website.

      h3 1.1 Technical Information
      p When you access the Website, our servers and hosting infrastructure may automatically receive certain technical information, including:
      ul
        li IP address;
        li browser type and version;
        li operating system;
        li device type;
        li referring website or URL;
        li pages visited;
        li date and time of access;
        li approximate geographic location derived from IP address;
        li information about how you interact with the Website.
      p This information is primarily used to operate, maintain, secure, and improve the Website.

      h3 1.2 Information You Voluntarily Provide
      p If the Website provides forms, newsletter subscriptions, contact forms, or other features that allow you to submit information, we may collect the information you choose to provide, such as:
      ul
        li name;
        li email address;
        li message or other information contained in your submission.
      p We only use such information for the purpose for which it was provided or as otherwise described at the time of collection.

      h2 2. Cookies and Similar Technologies
      p The Website may use cookies and similar technologies.
      p Cookies are small text files stored on your device that help websites remember information and understand how visitors use the Website.
      p We may use cookies for purposes including:
      ul
        li essential Website functionality;
        li security and fraud prevention;
        li remembering preferences;
        li measuring Website traffic and performance;
        li understanding which content is most useful to our readers;
        li improving the Website.
      p Some third-party services integrated into the Website may also use cookies or similar technologies.
      p You can control or disable cookies through your browser settings. Disabling certain cookies may affect the functionality of some parts of the Website.

      h2 3. Analytics
      p We may use analytics and measurement technologies to understand how visitors use the Website.
      p Analytics information may include pages viewed, approximate location, device information, traffic sources, and general usage statistics.
      p Where analytics services are used, the relevant third-party provider may process information according to its own privacy policy.
      p We use analytics information primarily in an aggregated or statistical form to improve our content, Website structure, performance, and user experience.

      h2 4. How We Use Information
      p We may use collected information to:
      ul
        li operate and maintain the Website;
        li provide access to news and other content;
        li improve the Website and its functionality;
        li understand Website traffic and audience interests;
        li detect and prevent abuse, fraud, spam, and security incidents;
        li diagnose technical problems;
        li respond to inquiries;
        li comply with applicable laws and legal obligations.
      p We do not use personal information for purposes incompatible with those described in this Privacy Policy without providing appropriate notice where required by law.

      h2 5. News Content and External Sources
      p Lyzfol publishes news, commentary, summaries, and other informational content.
      p Some content may contain links to third-party websites, publications, social media platforms, or other external resources.
      p When you follow an external link, you leave our Website and become subject to the privacy practices and terms of the third-party website.
      p We are not responsible for the privacy policies, security, or content of third-party websites.
      p We recommend reviewing the privacy policy of any external website you visit.

      h2 6. Advertising
      p If advertising is displayed on the Website, advertising providers may use cookies, pixels, or similar technologies to deliver, measure, or personalize advertisements.
      p Third-party advertising providers may collect information about your browser, device, IP address, and interactions with advertisements in accordance with their own privacy policies.
      p Where required by applicable law, we will provide appropriate mechanisms for managing consent or advertising preferences.

      h2 7. Data Sharing
      p We do not sell your personal information.
      p We may share limited information with third parties when necessary to operate the Website, including:
      ul
        li hosting and infrastructure providers;
        li analytics providers;
        li security and anti-abuse providers;
        li email or communication providers, where applicable;
        li advertising providers, where applicable;
        li professional advisers or service providers acting on our behalf.
      p We may also disclose information when required to do so by law, court order, governmental request, or when reasonably necessary to protect our rights, users, property, or the security of the Website.

      h2 8. Data Retention
      p We retain information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy, including operating the Website, maintaining security, complying with legal obligations, and resolving disputes.
      p Technical logs may be retained for periods necessary for security, troubleshooting, and operational purposes.
      p The exact retention period may vary depending on the type of information and the purpose for which it was collected.

      h2 9. Data Security
      p We take reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect information against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction.
      p However, no method of transmitting or storing information over the Internet can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
      p Therefore, we cannot guarantee absolute security of information transmitted to or through the Website.

      h2 10. Your Privacy Rights
      p Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have certain rights regarding your personal information.
      p These may include the right to:
      ul
        li request access to personal information we hold about you;
        li request correction of inaccurate information;
        li request deletion of your personal information;
        li object to certain processing;
        li request restriction of processing;
        li withdraw consent where processing is based on consent;
        li request information about how your personal information is processed;
        li lodge a complaint with a relevant data protection authority.
      p To exercise applicable rights, please contact us using the contact information provided below.
      p We may need to verify your request before taking action.

      h2 11. European Economic Area and GDPR
      p If you are located in the European Economic Area (“EEA”), United Kingdom, or another jurisdiction where similar data protection rights apply, you may have additional rights under applicable data protection legislation, including the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).
      p Where applicable, we process personal information on legal bases such as:
      ul
        li your consent;
        li performance of a service requested by you;
        li compliance with legal obligations;
        li our legitimate interests, provided that those interests are not overridden by your rights and freedoms.
      p Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw your consent at any time.

      h2 12. Children's Privacy
      p The Website is not intended to knowingly collect personal information from children.
      p We do not knowingly collect personal information from children without an appropriate legal basis or parental consent where such consent is required by law.
      p If you believe that a child has provided personal information to us, please contact us so that we can take appropriate steps.

      h2 13. Changes to This Privacy Policy
      p We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our Website, services, technology, or legal requirements.
      p When we make changes, we will update the “Last updated” date at the top of this page.
      p We encourage visitors to review this Privacy Policy periodically.

      h2 14. Contact Us
      p If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, your personal information, or the privacy practices of the Website, please contact us:
      ul.legal__contact
        li
          strong Website:
          =< link_to 'https://lyzfol.com/', 'https://lyzfol.com/'
        li
          strong Email:
          =< mail_to 'mykolalyzanets@gmail.com'
        li
          strong Publisher / Website Operator:
          |  Mykola Lyzanets

      h2 15. Acceptance of This Privacy Policy
      p By using the Website, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy.
      p If you do not agree with this Privacy Policy, please discontinue use of the Website.

    p.legal__copy © 2026 Lyzfol. All rights reserved.
